THIRD-PARTY INSPIRATIONS AND ATTRIBUTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

While FreeCAD Tutor MCP is an independent implementation tailored for tutoring
with FreeCAD 1.0/1.1+ and Claude Desktop on Windows, its design and several
engineering patterns were directly inspired by the following open-source projects:

1. theosib/FreeCAD-MCP-Server
   URL:     https://github.com/theosib/FreeCAD-MCP-Server
   Author:  Timothy Miller
   License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
   Notes:   Inspired the FreeCAD workbench addon + stdio MCP bridge split,
            newline-delimited TCP JSON-RPC 2.0 framing, and deep inspection
            toolset (list_documents, get_document_graph, inspect_object,
            analyze_shape, get_sketch_diagnostics, tracked_recompute,
            execute_script).

2. neka-nat/freecad-mcp
   URL:     https://github.com/neka-nat/freecad-mcp
   Author:  Shirokuma (k tanaka)
   License: MIT
   Notes:   Inspired the hardened Qt main-thread GUI dispatch patterns in
            freecad_addon/rpc_server.py (modeled after gui_dispatch.py:
            per-call response queues, QueuedConnection wake signals, bounded
            mouse-drag deferral) and the crash-safe Gui.activeView() /
            saveImage guard in freecad_addon/handlers/viewport.py (modeled
            after view_manager.py).

3. spkane/freecad-addon-robust-mcp-server
   URL:     https://github.com/spkane/freecad-addon-robust-mcp-server
   Author:  Sean P. Kane and contributors
   License: Apache-2.0 AND MIT
   Notes:   Inspired selection and workbench controls (get_selection,
            set_selection, list_workbenches, activate_workbench), Report view
            console capture (get_console_output), FreeCAD undo transaction
            wrappers (undo, redo, get_undo_redo_status), FreeCAD 1.x
            AttachmentSupport compatibility handling, and shared-token local
            RPC authentication.

4. sergiudanstan/freecad-mcp
   URL:     https://github.com/sergiudanstan/freecad-mcp
   Author:  Dan Stan
   License: MIT
   Notes:   Inspired TechDraw drawing creation/export workflows and broad
            Part / PartDesign / Sketcher modeling coverage.

5. FreeCAD/FreeCAD
   URL:     https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD
   License: LGPL-2.1-or-later
   Notes:   Upstream FreeCAD 1.1 source tree referenced for C++/Python runtime
            APIs (SketchObjectPyImp.cpp, DocumentObjectPyImp.cpp,
            FeaturePad.cpp, FeaturePocket.cpp, PartDesign::Plane, App::VarSet,
            and TechDrawGui).

6. Additional Ecosystem Repositories Surveyed During Research
   - contextform/freecad-mcp (https://github.com/contextform/freecad-mcp)
   - bonninr/freecad_mcp (https://github.com/bonninr/freecad_mcp, MIT, Rodolfo Bonnin)
   - YunchaoYang/robust-freecad-mcp (https://github.com/YunchaoYang/robust-freecad-mcp)
